<% character = roll.player.character %><% used = character.items.used_since(roll.scene.created_at) %>In scene <%= roll.scene.position %> of <%= roll.scene.game_session.scene_budget %>, <%= roll.scene.part_of_the_story %>, <%= roll.player.name %> chose "<%= roll.choice.label %>": die <%= roll.value %>, modifier <%= format("%+d", roll.modifier) %>, statuses <%= format("%+d", roll.status_modifier) %>, total <%= roll.total %> against <%= roll.target %>. <%= roll.grade_label %>, margin <%= format("%+d", roll.margin) %>.<% if roll.grade == :narrow %> It works, but not for free: it costs <%= roll.player.name %> something on the way.<% elsif !roll.success? %> It does not work, and what goes wrong takes the story somewhere new instead of back for another try.<% end %>
<% if used.any? %>Used since the scene began, already applied: <%= used.map { |item| "#{item.name} (#{format("%+d", item.hp_effect)} health)" }.join(", ") %>.
<% end %><%= roll.player.name %> now: <%= character.sheet %>.
<% if (companions = roll.scene.companions).any? %>In the scene with <%= roll.player.name %>: <%= companions.map { it.character.portrait }.join("; ") %>.
<% end %><% if roll.scene.followed_by_the_last? %>The next scene is the last, and the story ends in <%= roll.scene.game_session.verdict %>. Tell only what this roll does, in a paragraph or two, and stop there: the ending belongs to that last scene.
<% else %>Tell only what this roll does, in a paragraph or two, and stop there: the next scene comes in my next message.
<% end %>